k Overflow questions --><section class="so-questions" style="background:#12121a;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:8px;padding:1.5rem;margin:2rem 0;"><h3 style="font-family:monospace;font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#e0e0e8;margin:0 0 1rem;">Community Questions</h3><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="margin:0.6rem 0;padding:0.75rem;background:#12121a;border-radius:6px;"><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/word-cloud+javascript" rel="noopener" style="color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.9rem;" target="_blank">How to generate a word cloud with JavaScript and Canvas?</a><span style="display:block;font-size:0.75rem;color:#e0e0e8;margin-top:0.25rem;">12 answers · tagged: javascript, word-cloud, canvas</span></li><li style="margin:0.6rem 0;padding:0.75rem;background:#12121a;border-radius:6px;"><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/tag-cloud+collision-detection" rel="noopener" style="color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.9rem;" target="_blank">Collision detection algorithm for tag cloud layout?</a><span style="display:block;font-size:0.75rem;color:#e0e0e8;margin-top:0.25rem;">7 answers · tagged: algorithm, collision-detection, layout</span></li><li style="margin:0.6rem 0;padding:0.75rem;background:#12121a;border-radius:6px;"><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/word-frequency+text-analysis" rel="noopener" style="color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.9rem;" target="_blank">Best approach for counting word frequencies in JavaScript?</a><span style="display:block;font-size:0.75rem;color:#e0e0e8;margin-top:0.25rem;">15 answers · tagged: javascript, frequency, text-analysis</span></li></ul></section><!-- FAQ --><div class="faq-section"><h2 id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">What is a word cloud?</div><div class="faq-a">A word cloud is a visual representation of text data where words are displayed in varying sizes based on their frequency of occurrence. The most frequently used words appear largest, making it easy to identify key themes and patterns in any body of text at a glance.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">How do I create a word cloud?</div><div class="faq-a">Paste your text into the input area or upload a.txt file. The tool automatically counts word frequencies, removes common stop words, and renders a word cloud on the canvas. You can customize colors, fonts, shapes, and the maximum number of words before generating.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">Can I export the word cloud as an image?</div><div class="faq-a">Yes. Click the Export PNG button to download your word cloud as a high-resolution PNG image. The exported image matches the canvas dimensions and includes all your customization settings.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">What are stop words and why are they removed?</div><div class="faq-a">Stop words are common words like the, is, at, and, or that appear frequently in any text but carry little meaning. Removing them ensures your word cloud highlights the meaningful content words rather than being dominated by grammatical filler.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">What color schemes are available?</div><div class="faq-a">The generator includes five color schemes: rainbow (full spectrum), monochrome (shades of green), warm (reds, oranges, yellows), cool (blues, greens, purples), and custom where you pick two colors and the tool interpolates between them.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">What shape masks can I use?</div><div class="faq-a">You can render your word cloud in four shapes: rectangle (fills the full canvas), circle, heart, and star. The shape mask constrains where words are placed, creating a visually distinctive output.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">Is there a word limit for the input text?</div><div class="faq-a">There is no strict limit on input text length. The tool processes the text entirely in your browser, so performance depends on your device. For best results with very large texts, you can adjust the max words slider to control how many unique words appear in the cloud.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">Is my text data private?</div><div class="faq-a">Yes. All processing happens in your browser using client-side JavaScript. Your text is never uploaded to any server. There are no analytics tracking your input, no cookies storing your data, and no server-side processing. Your content stays on your device.</div></div></div><!-- L05: E-E-A-T author box --><div style="max-width:700px;margin:2rem auto;padding:20px;background:#12121a;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:8px;display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;"><div style="width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;background:#12121a;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:1.2rem;color:#e0e0e8;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;">ML</div><div style="flex:1;min-width:200px;"><p style="margin:0;color:#e0e0e8;font-weight:500;">Michael Lip</p><p style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:0.8rem;color:#e0e0e8;">Developer and tool builder at zovo.one. Building free, private, client-side web tools.</p><p style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:0.75rem;color:#e0e0e8;">March 19, 2026</p></div></div><p style="text-align:center;color:#e0e0e8;font-size:0.8rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">March 19, 2026</p><p style="text-align:center;color:#e0e0e8;font-size:0.75rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0.5rem;">March 19, 2026 by Michael Lip</p><div class="update-history" style="max-width:700px;margin:1.5rem auto;padding:12px 16px;background:#12121a;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;"><p style="color:#e0e0e8;font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px;">Update History</p><p style="color:#e0e0e8;font-size:0.75rem;margin:0;line-height:1.6;"> March 19, 2026 - Initial release with full functionality March 19, 2026 - Added shape masks and custom color support March 19, 2026 - Performance and accessibility improvements </p></div><!-- L13: Wikipedia definition box --><div class="wiki-definition" style="max-width:700px;margin:1.5rem auto;padding:16px 20px;background:#12121a;border-left:4px solid #00ff88;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;"><p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-size:0.7rem;color:#e0e0e8;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.5px;">Wikipedia</p><p style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:0.9rem;color:#e0e0e8;line-height:1.6;">A tag cloud (also known as a word cloud or weighted list in visual design) is a visual representation of text data, typically used to depict keyword metadata (tags) on websites, or to visualize free form text. Tags are usually single words, and the importance of each tag is shown with font size or color.</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:0.7rem;color:#e0e0e8;">Source: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tag_cloud" rel="noopener" style="color:#e0e0e8;" target="_blank">Wikipedia - Tag cloud</a> · Verified March 19, 2026</p></div><!-- Privacy badge --><div style="text-align:center;margin:1.5rem 0;"><img alt="Privacy: 100% Client-Side" height="28" loading="lazy" src="https://img.shields.io/badge/privacy-100%25_client--side-00ff88?style=for-the-badge"/></div><!-- Related Tools --><div style="max-width:800px;margin:2rem auto;padding:1.5rem;"><div style="font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#e0e0e8;margin-bottom:0.75rem;font-weight:500;">Related Tools</div><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;"><a href="/free-tools/character-counter/" style="display:inline-block;padding:6px 14px;background:#12121a;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:6px;color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;">Character Counter</a><a href="/free-tools/word-counter/" style="display:inline-block;padding:6px 14px;background:#12121a;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:6px;color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;">Word Counter</a><a href="/free-tools/text-case-converter/" style="display:inline-block;padding:6px 14px;background:#12121a;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:6px;color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;">Text Case Converter</a><a href="/free-tools/lorem-ipsum-generator/" style="display:inline-block;padding:6px 14px;background:#12121a;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:6px;color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;">Lorem Ipsum Generator</a><a href="/free-tools/readability-checker/" style="display:inline-block;padding:6px 14px;background:#12121a;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:6px;color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;">Readability Checker</a><a href="/free-tools/paraphrase-tool/" style="display:inline-block;padding:6px 14px;background:#12121a;border:1px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:6px;color:#e0e0e8;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;">Paraphrase Tool</a></div></div></div><script> (function(){ // Stop words list var STOP_WORDS = new Set(['the','be','to','of','and','a','in','that','have','i','it','for','not','on','with','he','as','you','do','at','this','but','his','by','from','they','we','say','her','she','or','an','will','my','one','all','would','there','their','what','so','up','out','if','about','who','get','which','go','me','when','make','can','like','time','no','just','him','know','take','people','into','year','your','good','some','could','them','see','other','than','then','now','look','only','come','its','over','think','also','back','after','use','two','how','our','work','first','well','way','even','new','want','because','any','these','give','day','most','us','is','are','was','were','been','being','has','had','did','does','done','may','might','must','shall','should','very','much','more','many','each','every','such','here','where','why','let','still','own','too','same','both','another','through','during','before','between','under','again','further','once','am','been','few','those','against','above','below','while','until','down','upon','already','since','often','around','however','always','never','perhaps','almost','rather','quite','really','yet','something','anything','everything','nothing','someone','anyone','everyone','long','last','old','great','little','big','right','high','different','small','large','next','early','young','important','public','bad','off']); var maxWordsSlider = document.getElementById('max-words'); var maxWordsVal = document.getElementById('max-words-val'); maxWordsSlider.addEventListener('input', function(){ maxWordsVal.textContent = this.value; }); var colorSchemeSelect = document.getElementById('color-scheme'); var customColorsDiv = document.getElementById('custom-colors'); colorSchemeSelect.addEventListener('change', function(){ customColorsDiv.style.display = this.value === 'custom'? 'flex' : 'none'; }); document.getElementById('file-upload').addEventListener('change', function(e){ var file = e.target.files[0]; if(!file) return; document.getElementById('file-name').textContent = file.name; var reader = new FileReader(); reader.onload = function(ev){ document.getElementById('text-input').value = ev.target.result; }; reader.readAsText(file); }); function getWords(text){ var excludeStr = document.getElementById('exclude-words').value.toLowerCase(); var excludeSet = new Set(); if(excludeStr){ excludeStr.split(',').forEach(function(w){ var t=w.trim(); if(t) excludeSet.add(t); }); } var minFreq = parseInt(document.getElementById('min-freq').value) || 1; var words = text.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z\s'-]/g, ' ').split(/\s+/).filter(function(w){ return w.length > 1; }); var freq = {}; words.forEach(function(w){ w = w.replace(/^['-]+|['-]+$/g, ''); if(w.length < 2) return; if(STOP_WORDS.has(w)) return; if(excludeSet.has(w)) return; freq[w] = (freq[w] || 0) + 1; }); var sorted = Object.entries(freq).filter(function(e){ return e[1] >= minFreq; }).sort(function(a,b){ return b[1]-a[1]; }); var maxW = parseInt(maxWordsSlider.value) || 100; return sorted.slice(0, maxW); } function getColorForIndex(i, total){ var scheme = colorSchemeSelect.value; var t = total > 1? i / (total - 1) : 0; if(scheme === 'rainbow'){ var hue = Math.round(t * 360); return 'hsl(' + hue + ', 80%, 60%)'; } else if(scheme === 'monochrome'){ var l = 40 + Math.round(t * 35); return 'hsl(145, 80%, ' + l + '%)'; } else if(scheme === 'warm'){ var hue2 = Math.round(t * 60); return 'hsl(' + hue2 + ', 85%, 55%)'; } else if(scheme === 'cool'){ var hue3 = 180 + Math.round(t * 100); return 'hsl(' + hue3 + ', 70%, 55%)'; } else { var c1 = document.getElementById('color1').value; var c2 = document.getElementById('color2').value; var r1=parseInt(c1.slice(1,3),16), g1=parseInt(c1.slice(3,5),16), b1=parseInt(c1.slice(5,7),16); var r2=parseInt(c2.slice(1,3),16), g2=parseInt(c2.slice(3,5),16), b2=parseInt(c2.slice(5,7),16); var r=Math.round(r1+(r2-r1)*t), g=Math.round(g1+(g2-g1)*t), b=Math.round(b1+(b2-b1)*t); return 'rgb('+r+','+g+','+b+')'; } } function isInShape(x, y, w, h, shape){ var cx = w/2, cy = h/2; if(shape === 'rectangle') return true; if(shape === 'circle'){ var rx = w/2 * 0.95, ry = h/2 * 0.95; return ((x-cx)*(x-cx))/(rx*rx) + ((y-cy)*(y-cy))/(ry*ry) <= 1; } if(shape === 'heart'){ var nx = (x - cx) / (w/2); var ny = (cy - y) / (h/2) - 0.2; return (nx*nx + ny*ny - 1)*(nx*nx + ny*ny - 1)*(nx*nx + ny*ny - 1) - nx*nx*ny*ny*ny < 0.02; } if(shape === 'star'){ var angle = Math.atan2(y - cy, x - cx); var dist = Math.sqrt((x-cx)*(x-cx) + (y-cy)*(y-cy)); var maxR = Math.min(w, h) * 0.45; var starAngle = angle + Math.PI/2; var r = maxR * (0.5 + 0.5 * Math.abs(Math.cos(2.5 * starAngle))); return dist <= r; } return true; } window.generateCloud = function(){ var text = document.getElementById('text-input').value; if(!text.trim()){ alert('Please enter some text first.'); return; } var wordData = getWords(text); if(wordData.length === 0){ alert('No words found after filtering. Try lowering the minimum frequency or adding more text.'); return; } var canvas = document.getElementById('cloud-canvas'); var ctx = canvas.getContext('2d'); var W = canvas.width, H = canvas.height; var shape = document.getElementById('shape-select').value; var font = document.getElementById('font-select').value; ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H); ctx.fillStyle = ''; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H); var maxCount = wordData[0][1]; var minCount = wordData[wordData.length - 1][1]; var placed = []; for(var i = 0; i < wordData.length; i++){ var word = wordData[i][0]; var count = wordData[i][1]; var ratio = maxCount > minCount? (count - minCount) / (maxCount - minCount) : 1; var fontSize = Math.max(12, Math.round(14 + ratio * 52)); ctx.font = fontSize + 'px ' + font; var metrics = ctx.measureText(word); var tw = metrics.width + 4; var th = fontSize + 4; var didPlace = false; var cx = W/2, cy = H/2; var spiralStep = 0; for(var attempt = 0; attempt < 2000; attempt++){ var angle = spiralStep * 0.15; var radius = 2 + spiralStep * 0.8; var px = cx + radius * Math.cos(angle) - tw/2; var py = cy + radius * Math.sin(angle) - th/2; spiralStep++; if(px < 2 || py < 2 || px + tw > W - 2 || py + th > H - 2) continue; if(!isInShape(px + tw/2, py + th/2, W, H, shape)) continue; var overlap = false; for(var j = 0; j < placed.length; j++){ var p = placed[j]; if(!(px + tw < p.x || px > p.x + p.w || py + th < p.y || py > p.y + p.h)){ overlap = true; break; } } if(!overlap){ var color = getColorForIndex(i, wordData.length); ctx.fillStyle = color; ctx.font = fontSize + 'px ' + font; ctx.fillText(word, px + 2, py + fontSize); placed.push({x: px, y: py, w: tw, h: th}); didPlace = true; break; } } } // Show frequency table var totalWords = wordData.reduce(function(s,e){ return s + e[1]; }, 0); var tbody = document.getElementById('freq-body'); tbody.innerHTML = ''; wordData.forEach(function(entry, idx){ var tr = document.createElement('tr'); var pct = ((entry[1] / totalWords) * 100).toFixed(1); tr.innerHTML = '<td style="color:#e0e0e8;">' + (idx+1) + '</td><td>' + entry[0] + '</td><td style="color:#e0e0e8;">' + entry[1] + '</td><td><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;"><div style="background:#12121a;height:6px;border-radius:3px;width:' + Math.max(4, pct * 2) + 'px;"></div><span style="color:#e0e0e8;font-size:0.8rem;">' + pct + '%</span></div></td>'; tbody.appendChild(tr); }); document.getElementById('freq-container').style.display = 'block'; }; window.exportPNG = function(){ var canvas = document.getElementById('cloud-canvas'); var link = document.createElement('a'); link.download = 'word-cloud.png'; link.href = canvas.toDataURL('image/png'); link.click(); }; window.clearAll = function(){ document.getElementById('text-input').value = ''; document.getElementById('exclude-words').value = ''; document.getElementById('file-name').textContent = ''; var canvas = document.getElementById('cloud-canvas'); var ctx = canvas.getContext('2d'); ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height); ctx.fillStyle = ''; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height); document.getElementById('freq-container').style.display = 'none'; }; // FAQ toggle document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach(function(item){ item.querySelector('.faq-q').addEventListener('click', function(){ item.classList.toggle('open'); }); }); })(); </script><script> (function(){ // Stop words list var STOP_WORDS = new Set(['the','be','to','of','and','a','in','that','have','i','it','for','not','on','with','he','as','you','do','at','this','but','his','by','from','they','we','say','her','she','or','an','will','my','one','all','would','there','their','what','so','up','out','if','about','who','get','which','go','me','when','make','can','like','time','no','just','him','know','take','people','into','year','your','good','some','could','them','see','other','than','then','now','look','only','come','its','over','think','also','back','after','use','two','how','our','work','first','well','way','even','new','want','because','any','these','give','day','most','us','is','are','was','were','been',